# Runtime image build context. The Dockerfile COPYs `app/` (base) and `tests/`
# (dev stage) explicitly, so exclude everything that must never enter an image
# or would bust the build cache.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Python / caches. `**/`: a bare pattern matches only at the context ROOT, so the host's
# app/**/__pycache__ (and app/.DS_Store) shipped in every image until this was anchored.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Secrets / env — must NEVER enter the image (only .env.example is harmless), at any depth:
# `COPY app` takes app/ whole, and the clean-tree gate never sees a gitignored file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime output (bind-mounted at runtime, never baked)
**/output/

# Release documents: repo history, not runtime. The runtime COPYs `app/` whole, so without
# these lines every published image carried every change log, including any detail a later
# scrub removed from the repo.
app/change_logs/
app/release_notes/

# Docs / dashboards (not needed in the runtime image)
docs/
grafana/
*.md

# Compose / Dockerfiles / build tooling
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
Makefile

# OS / editor
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude
.claude/
